# Concept Content Factory — working rules

You are in a Python 3.11+ repository. **Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/SETUP.md` first.** Do not
assume any particular AI vendor: the factory's text roles run on whatever model provider the
operator configured (`.env`, see below).

## Set up / run
- `scripts/setup.sh` creates `.venv`, installs the package and creates `.env` from `.env.example`.
- Choose the model for every text role (any provider; prices per 1M tokens are the user's to give):
  `python configure_llm.py xai --model <name> --input-price <n> --output-price <n>`
  (`--list` shows presets; `ollama` + `--free` for a local model).
- The API key goes in `.env` (or the shell) under the variable the command prints — never in code,
  never in a commit, never echoed back.
- `python check_llm.py` makes one tiny real call; `python doctor.py [clipping|posting|generation]`
  reports what the machine still lacks. Entrypoints read `.env` themselves.

## Change code
- Quality gate, all green before a change is done:
  `ruff check . && ruff format --check . && mypy && pytest -q`
- Spec/ADR before code (`docs/adr/`); documents win over code (`PROJECT.md` §17).
- Extend additively. Do not change `Run`'s existing behaviour; do not hardcode a model, a price or
  a token budget; no new dependency without need (vendor adapters use stdlib `urllib`).
- Only `infrastructure/` may do I/O or import third-party packages (`tests/test_adapter_contract.py`).

## Never
- Publish, post or upload anything without the user explicitly asking in this conversation.
- Print, log or commit a secret.
